issue('unintroduced-P0','The illustration defining nu_k on page 14 uses P^0 without a definition there. That symbol is preserved as an unresolved source convention.',[14])
issue('lp-notation','The stated general Lp norm lacks absolute values and the infinity-endpoint convention, although p ranges through infinity. The actual theorem uses L2. Preserve the printed general definition.',[9])
issue('regularity-external','Asymptotic linearity and efficient influence function are described in the main text, but regularity and full model/tangent-space definitions are not provided. Supplementary efficiency exposition remains excluded.',[9])
issue('efficient-identification-conditions','The paragraph identifying D_GSC and D_SC as efficient influence functions requires DS.0 plus two-sided ratio bounds or DS.0-dagger plus bounded odds. These conditions qualify that source identification; they must not be silently inserted into all of Theorem 1.',[13,17,18])
